&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you’ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the Spend Conversion function from the ground up, defining the strategy, entry criteria, engagement model, and KPIs for converting non-card vendor spend to Brex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Envision a holistic approach involving key parties and operations from Capital One as well as 3rd party vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end vendor spend migration motion, from vendor-file analysis and card-acceptance identification through negotiation and card activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with product, implementation, BD, and sales to bring these workflows to market, and to grow our acceptance database through data partnerships, not just outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise enterprise customers directly, unlocking spend with their most strategic vendors and translating their goals into concrete migration and negotiation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence RFPs and other evaluations of Brex by prospective customers; drive confidence in Brex’s Suppler Enablement program and best-in-class capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a differentiated, AI-native approach to supplier enablement rather than replicating the manual playbook legacy issuers rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the operational rigor (tracking, reporting, and incentive structures) that makes the function measurable and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and coach a team of specialists as the function proves out, operating as a player-coach in the early phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion spend conversion internally, educating stakeholders and shaping how Brex captures share-of-wallet across its customer base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in B2B/commercial card, payments, supplier enablement, or vendor/payment operations, deep enough to shorten the learning curve, rather than learning the domain on the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building a function or program from 0-to-1 (or scaling something early and unstructured), standing up processes, KPIs, and operating cadences where little existed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of card acceptance and merchant economics: how vendors process cards, card-on-file vs. card-per-invoice, fees, and the buyer/supplier trade-offs (e.g., DSO/DPO, cash flow).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to negotiate and influence, with vendors on acceptance terms and internally across executives and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct customer-facing experience with enterprise customers; comfort owning senior relationships and turning customer goals into execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A first-principles, builder mentality: you create the vision and drive it forward through ambiguity rather than waiting for a playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record as a cross-functional operator who has shipped alongside product, sales/BD, and implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A leadership foundation: you&#39;ve led people or major initiatives and are ready to build and manage a team over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
