&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This opportunity is on our Product Data Platform (PDP) team, which builds and operates the high-performance data, query, and search infrastructure that powers critical Brex product experiences, including AI-powered data products like our agentic reporting experience. PDP&#39;s mission is to make Brex customizable, scalable, and reliable for finance teams, and that requires deeply optimized, production-grade distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer, you&#39;ll shape the technical direction of the platform across multiple teams. Your mandate is to identify the highest-impact architectural problems across the data products group, including the cross-cutting ones that fall between teams, and drive them to resolution. You&#39;ll be accountable for the group&#39;s technical quality, move between long-horizon strategy and hands-on execution, and lead through influence rather than authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical strategy for critical PDP initiatives, balancing long-term architecture with near-term delivery across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve systemic performance, consistency, and scalability problems, including cross-team gaps no single team can own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own architecture direction for query performance: query plans, execution paths, cost models, indexing strategies, and schema and access-pattern design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve distributed systems with thoughtful tradeoffs around consistency, latency, caching, cost, and failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the technical bar across the group through design reviews and architecture decisions, and dive in hands-on where it matters most, including P95/P99 latency issues in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify scaling risks and reliability gaps, and turn findings into plans the group aligns behind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor senior engineers and grow the next generation of technical leaders within PDP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly on high-stakes initiatives and critical path decisions, primarily in the JVM ecosystem (Kotlin/Java).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating production systems at scale, including as a technical leader on multi-team initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading architecture and delivery for large-scale distributed systems in a platform or infrastructure environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise with relational databases (Postgres or Aurora strongly preferred), including query plan analysis, indexing strategies, and real-world optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive ambiguous, cross-cutting problems to resolution without a defined charter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, with the ability to influence stakeholders and align teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with OpenSearch / Elasticsearch or similar systems in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with streaming data platforms (Flink, Kafka) or semantic/analytics layers in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-tenant or data-heavy platforms in regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform foundations for AI or agentic product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $240,000 - $300,000 CAD. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
